  "next_id": 44,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -30,
        -34
      ],
      "id": 43,
      "text": "Maximum power point tracking (Perturb & Observe) on a 10 W solar panel.\nThe Blue Pill sets the current of an electronic load (U2, Q1, R3 = 1 ohm) with a filtered PWM (PA0, R5, R6, C1),\nreads the panel voltage (PA1, R1/R2) and the current (PA2, 1 mV per mA), and moves the duty by 1 % every 50 ms towards more power.\nWhile running, drag PV1 (irradiance) or use Shift with the wheel (cell temperature): the symbol shows the power as % of the maximum.\nAnalyzer > UART: \"V <mV> mV I <mA> mA P <mW> mW D <duty> %\" every 250 ms.\nA real MPPT feeds a DC-DC converter instead of a load; the algorithm is the same."
    }
  ],
